      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 63-year-old woman was referred to the gastroenterology outpatient clinic with gallstones and a big liver mass on ultrasound. She had episodes of upper abdominal pain. Magnetic resonance imaging showed typical images for a giant liver haemangioma. We performed a surgical resection of the giant haemangioma and the gallbladder."},
